{"duration_api_ms":502240,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"69f98006-d98a-4e91-abc9-74ef1b293372","total_cost_usd":2.1269006,"usage":{"input_tokens":152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98936,"cache_read_input_tokens":6761883,"output_tokens":36878,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16620},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98936,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2993,"cache_read_input_tokens":114068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1892},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9586,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009696000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":152,"outputTokens":36878,"cacheReadInputTokens":6761883,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98936,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.1172045999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":16620,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":100,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured VLAN access-port segmentation on node1 (SONiC) separating node2's segment (eth1, VLAN 101) from node3's segment (eth2, VLAN 102) using the kernel-level vlan-aware \\\"Bridge\\\" device already present on SONiC-VS, since the Ethernet* SAI port abstraction is unbound from the real virtio NICs. eth1 and eth2 are untagged/PVID access ports in VLAN 101 and 102 respectively; node1 holds an SVI (Bridge.101 = 192.168.101.1/24, Bridge.102 = 192.168.102.1/24) giving it a working L3 link into each VLAN, while node2 (192.168.101.2/24 on enp8s0) and node3 (192.168.102.2/24 on enp8s0) cannot reach each other (different subnets, no cross-VLAN forwarding, ip_forward disabled on node1). Physical topology was first identified experimentally (eth1<->node2, eth2<->node3) via temporary IP/ping tests. Node2/node3 IP configs were made persistent via NetworkManager connection profiles (autoconnect) after discovering NM was clobbering ad hoc `ip addr` assignments on enp8s0. Node1's VLAN/bridge state was made persistent via a new enabled systemd oneshot unit (vlan-access-segmentation.service) that reapplies the configuration at boot, since raw `ip`/`bridge` state on SONiC-VS does not survive reboot and the Ethernet* configdb path isn't usable for these NICs. Ran the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured pre-restart boot_id and healthy-state evidence, restarted each node individually (node1 via `reboot`, node2/node3 via `systemctl reboot`), confirmed changed boot_id and full recovery (VLAN config, IP config, and connectivity/isolation all confirmed intact) before moving to the next node. A benign duplicate-ICMP-reply artifact (0% packet loss, cosmetic DUP! in ping output) was observed and investigated; it is caused by the underlying nested-virtualization dataplane, not the VLAN configuration, and does not affect isolation or link correctness.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected topology on node1 (SONiC), node2, node3 via ip -br link/addr/route\",\"Identified physical mapping eth1<->node2 and eth2<->node3 via temporary IP + ping tests\",\"Cleaned up docker0 class-E leak on node1 per SONiC reference\",\"Added eth1/eth2 as members of node1's existing vlan-aware kernel 'Bridge' device\",\"Set eth1 PVID untagged VLAN 101, eth2 PVID untagged VLAN 102 via `bridge vlan add`\",\"Created Bridge.101 and Bridge.102 SVIs with IPs 192.168.101.1/24 and 192.168.102.1/24 for node1's presence in each VLAN\",\"Disabled net.ipv4.ip_forward on node1 to prevent inter-VLAN routing\",\"Diagnosed and fixed NetworkManager clobbering manual enp8s0 IPs on node2/node3 by creating persistent 'Wired connection 2' profiles with static IPs 192.168.101.2/24 and 192.168.102.2/24\",\"Verified node1<->node2 and node1<->node3 connectivity, and node2<->node3 isolation\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/vlan-access-segmentation.sh and a new systemd unit vlan-access-segmentation.service on node1, enabled at boot for persistence\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time using native reboot mechanisms, polling each until command execution resumed\",\"Verified changed boot_id and full post-restart recovery of VLAN config, IP config, connectivity, and isolation on all three nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline topology mapping (eth1<->node2, eth2<->node3)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f3ef99a8bc014532\",\"cmd-21fbf3f7b2024df7\",\"cmd-9a785ce086084c6e\"],\"summary\":\"Temporary IP assignment + ping confirmed eth1 reaches node2 and eth2 reaches node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"eth1/eth2 configured as untagged access ports in separate VLANs\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-777fdc4fba3e4ab1\",\"cmd-1108ec232bf74950\"],\"summary\":\"bridge vlan show confirms eth1=VLAN101 PVID untagged, eth2=VLAN102 PVID untagged\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 keeps a working link to each host inside its own VLAN\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8b14513d869a4202\",\"cmd-69d5186ca9b34024\",\"cmd-aef844fbcbba4a2b\"],\"summary\":\"Bidirectional pings between node1's Bridge.101/Bridge.102 SVIs and node2/node3 succeed with 0% loss, pre- and post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 remain isolated from each other\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7cf397ac0ecb4486\",\"cmd-e5e2dde0443e45cc\",\"cmd-dbe573e0eceb4fe8\",\"cmd-66f536ea3e884567\"],\"summary\":\"Cross-subnet pings between node2 and node3 fail (Destination Net Unreachable) both before and after node restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6f83defd1a324a99\",\"cmd-c27013416003494c\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 boot_id ce04f497... plus working VLAN/bridge state and ip_forward=0 prior to reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-63a6a4ac5f9149d3\",\"cmd-6d143629d064436d\",\"cmd-2a0560a618474a25\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged, connection reset confirmed disruption, and new boot_id c26dac0f... proves the restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of VLAN config and connectivity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e9eb7f07985c4b05\",\"cmd-c27013416003494c\",\"cmd-bc632ec049034b03\",\"cmd-c15571f12b9b41f5\"],\"summary\":\"vlan-access-segmentation.service reapplied Bridge/VLAN/SVI config automatically at boot; ip_forward remained 0; node2 and node3 could ping node1 again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1a7a413860e44b73\",\"cmd-dd74eeaf60314ee6\",\"cmd-a5e218fcf80148c0\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id d4784d1b... baseline, issued systemctl reboot, and confirmed new boot_id ed91ff51... after recovery\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-33738545f2cd46cf\",\"cmd-dbe573e0eceb4fe8\"],\"summary\":\"enp8s0 static IP persisted via NetworkManager autoconnect profile; ping to node1 succeeded; isolation from node3 held\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, and changed boot identity\",\"comma