t`), confirmed changed boot_id and full recovery (VLAN config, IP config, and connectivity/isolation all confirmed intact) before moving to the next node. A benign duplicate-ICMP-reply artifact (0% packet loss, cosmetic DUP! in ping output) was observed and investigated; it is caused by the underlying nested-virtualization dataplane, not the VLAN configuration, and does not affect isolation or link correctness.","actions_performed":["Inspected topology on node1 (SONiC), node2, node3 via ip -br link/addr/route","Identified physical mapping eth1<->node2 and eth2<->node3 via temporary IP + ping tests","Cleaned up docker0 class-E leak on node1 per SONiC reference","Added eth1/eth2 as members of node1's existing vlan-aware kernel 'Bridge' device","Set eth1 PVID untagged VLAN 101, eth2 PVID untagged VLAN 102 via `bridge vlan add`","Created Bridge.101 and Bridge.102 SVIs with IPs 192.168.101.1/24 and 192.168.102.1/24 for node1's presence in each VLAN","Disabled net.ipv4.ip_forward on node1 to prevent inter-VLAN routing","Diagnosed and fixed NetworkManager clobbering manual enp8s0 IPs on node2/node3 by creating persistent 'Wired connection 2' profiles with static IPs 192.168.101.2/24 and 192.168.102.2/24","Verified node1<->node2 and node1<->node3 connectivity, and node2<->node3 isolation","Wrote /usr/local/bin/vlan-access-segmentation.sh and a new systemd unit vlan-access-segmentation.service on node1, enabled at boot for persistence","Captured pre-restart boot_id and health baseline on all three nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time using native reboot mechanisms, polling each until command execution resumed","Verified changed boot_id and full post-restart recovery of VLAN config, IP config, connectivity, and isolation on all three nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline topology mapping (eth1<->node2, eth2<->node3)","command_ids":["cmd-f3ef99a8bc014532","cmd-21fbf3f7b2024df7","cmd-9a785ce086084c6e"],"summary":"Temporary IP assignment + ping confirmed et